cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Drydock: reproducible high-throughput virtual screening"
message: "If you use Drydock in your research, please cite it and the underlying docking engines."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Drydock contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<user>/drydock"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Drydock prepares compound libraries and runs batch molecular docking against a
  prepared receptor, producing a ranked CSV of affinities joined to compound
  descriptors. Screening runs as a detached, resumable process with pinned
  dependencies and deterministic per-ligand seeds, so results reproduce across
  machines. Supports AutoDock Vina, Vinardo, and the AutoDock4/AutoDock4Zn
  scoring functions.
keywords:
  - virtual screening
  - molecular docking
  - AutoDock Vina
  - AutoDock4Zn
  - cheminformatics
  - reproducibility

